#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:2
msgid "Defining tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:4
msgid ""
"Poe the Poet supports several ways of defining tasks under :toml:`[tool.poe."
"tasks]`, trading off simplicity against configurability. Furthermore toml "
"syntax supports both more terse or more expressive alternative ways of "
"writing the same thing, see the guide on :doc:`../guides/toml_guide` for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:6
msgid ""
"A task defined as a string will by default be interpreted as a single "
"command to be executed without a shell (aka a :doc:`cmd task <task_types/"
"cmd>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:8
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"test = \"pytest\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:13
msgid ""
"A task defined as an array will by default be interpreted as a :doc:"
"`sequence <task_types/sequence>` of :doc:`references<task_types/ref>` to "
"other tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:15
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"test   = \"pytest\"\n"
"_build = \"poetry build\"\n"
"build  = [\"test\", \"_build\"] # this task runs the two referenced tasks in "
"sequence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:24
msgid ""
"Task with names starting with an underscore ``_`` are excluded from "
"documentation and cannot be run directly from the command line. They can "
"only be run when referenced by another task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:26
msgid ""
"Tasks can also be defined as sub-tables, which allows for specifying the "
"task type and various configuration options on the task. The type of a task "
"defined as a table is determined by the presence of a particular key that is "
"unique to a certain task type and corresponds to the name of the task type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:28
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.test-quick]\n"
"help = \"Run tests excluding those makes as slow.\"\n"
"cmd  = \"pytest -m \\\"not slow\\\"\" # here the cmd key identifies the task "
"type and content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:34
msgid ""
"This implies that you can also define tasks of other types on a single line, "
"like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:36
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks]\n"
"tunnel.shell = \"ssh -N -L 0.0.0.0:8080:$PROD:8080 $PROD &\" # (posix) shell "
"based task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:41
msgid ""
":doc:`Some options <options>` are applicable to all tasks, whereas other are "
"only applicable to :ref:`specific types of tasks<Types of task>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:45
msgid ""
"Top level tasks are defined as members of :toml:`[tool.poe.tasks]`, but "
"sometimes tasks can be defined as children of other tasks, for example as "
"items within a :doc:`sequence <task_types/sequence>` task, or as the "
"``control`` or ``case`` roles within a :doc:`switch <task_types/switch>` "
"task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:48
msgid "Types of task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:50
msgid ""
"There are two categories of task each including four types: *Execution "
"tasks* that run task content in a subprocess, and *Orchestration tasks* that "
"run other tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:53
msgid "Execution tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:55
msgid ""
":doc:`Command tasks <task_types/cmd>` :code:`cmd` : for simple commands that "
"are executed as a subprocess without a shell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:57
msgid ""
":doc:`Script tasks<task_types/script>` :code:`script` : for python function "
"calls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:59
msgid ""
":doc:`Shell tasks<task_types/shell>` :code:`shell` : for scripts to be "
"executed with via an external interpreter (such as bash)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:61
msgid ""
":doc:`Expression tasks<task_types/expr>` :code:`expr` : which consist of a "
"python expression to evaluate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:64
msgid "Orchestration tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:66
msgid ""
":doc:`Sequence tasks<task_types/sequence>` :code:`sequence` : for composing "
"multiple tasks into a sequence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:68
msgid ""
":doc:`Parallel tasks<task_types/parallel>` :code:`parallel` : for running "
"multiple tasks concurrently"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:70
msgid ""
":doc:`Switch tasks<task_types/switch>` :code:`switch` : for running "
"different tasks depending on the output of a *control* task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tasks/index.rst:72
msgid ""
":doc:`Reference tasks<task_types/ref>` :code:`ref` : for defining a task as "
"an alias of another task, such as in a sequence task"
msgstr ""
